{{- /*
  Complete GitHub feedback collection. Kept at the existing fragment name for
  the babysitters; pr-fetch-comments also consumes it for standalone prompts.
  Each connection is paginated independently, including nested thread replies.
*/ -}}
`gh pr view --json reviewThreads` is **not supported** — use GraphQL. Resolve
<owner>, <repo>, and <number> to the target PR before running these commands.
Use the configured GitHub account; inspect only identity metadata, never tokens.

```bash
gh pr view <number> --repo <owner>/<repo> --json author,headRefOid,url

# All threads, with the first PAGE of comments (not just the first comment).
gh api graphql --paginate --slurp -f query='
query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
    pullRequest(number:$number) {
      reviewThreads(first:100, after:$endCursor) {
        pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        nodes {
          id isResolved isOutdated
          comments(first:100) {
            pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
            nodes {
              id url body createdAt updatedAt
              author { login __typename }
              path line originalLine
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}' -F owner=<owner> -F name=<repo> -F number=<number>
```

Outer pagination does **not** fetch nested pages. For EACH thread whose
comments.pageInfo.hasNextPage is true, fetch its complete comment connection
separately below and replace that thread's partial comments with the merged
pages (deduplicate by ID). <thread-id> is the GraphQL node ID from above.

```bash
gh api graphql --paginate --slurp -f query='
query($id:ID!,$endCursor:String) {
  node(id:$id) {
    ... on PullRequestReviewThread {
      comments(first:100, after:$endCursor) {
        pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        nodes {
          id url body createdAt updatedAt
          author { login __typename }
          path line originalLine
        }
      }
    }
  }
}' -f id=<thread-id>

# General PR comments, including author requests outside review threads.
gh api graphql --paginate --slurp -f query='
query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
    pullRequest(number:$number) {
      comments(first:100, after:$endCursor) {
        pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        nodes { id url body createdAt updatedAt author { login __typename } }
      }
    }
  }
}' -F owner=<owner> -F name=<repo> -F number=<number>

# Review summaries can also contain actionable requests.
gh api graphql --paginate --slurp -f query='
query($owner:String!,$name:String!,$number:Int!,$endCursor:String) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
    pullRequest(number:$number) {
      reviews(first:100, after:$endCursor) {
        pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        nodes { id url body createdAt updatedAt state author { login __typename } }
      }
    }
  }
}' -F owner=<owner> -F name=<repo> -F number=<number>
```

Check exit status AND GraphQL errors/null data for every page. Follow every
hasNextPage/endCursor until exhausted; --slurp produces an array of page
responses, not an array of comments. Do not infer zero feedback from a failed
or incomplete fetch: notify and retry later without marking it processed or
merging on an incomplete snapshot.

Set PR_AUTHOR_LOGIN from PR metadata. Build FEEDBACK_JSON from all pages:
source kind (thread / general comment / review summary), IDs/URLs, author
login/type, body, createdAt/updatedAt, thread resolution/outdated flags, and
path/line when present. Preserve every thread's chronological comments as
context, including the author's later replies. Deduplicate identical IDs and
group overlapping requests without losing their source links. Empty reviews
and acknowledgments need no change, but do not filter by author in retrieval.
